---
// wi.wickedagile.com — a redirect, deliberately.
//
// The standalone builder UI moved into wicked-studio; this package is now the ENGINE behind the
// creator surface (doc storage, version lineage, `data-wid` instrumentation, HTML/PDF/PPTX export,
// Playwright demo recording). Its own service says so to any direct visitor:
//
//   "This is the wicked-interactive bridge — it serves the API, not the UI."
//
// A product site still selling "point at the page, say the change" as a destination sent people to
// a front door that no longer opens. The package stays published — wicked-crew spawns it, and it
// is the sole implementation of that engine — but the SITE points at the surface people use.
//
// Kept as a real page rather than a bare meta-refresh so the reason is legible to anyone who lands
// here from an old link, a search result, or a bookmark.
const TARGET = 'https://ws.wickedagile.com';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>wicked-interactive has moved into wicked-studio</title>
    <meta name="description" content="The interactive builder is now part of wicked-studio — the orchestrator IDE. wicked-interactive continues as the engine behind it." />
    <link rel="canonical" href={TARGET} />
    <meta http-equiv="refresh" content={`3; url=${TARGET}`} />
    <style>
      :root { color-scheme: dark; }
      * { box-sizing: border-box; }
      body {
        margin: 0; min-height: 100svh; display: grid; place-items: center; padding: 24px;
        background: #0b1020; color: #e8ecff;
        font: 16px/1.6 ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
      }
      main { max-width: 44rem; text-align: left; }
      h1 { font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.2rem); line-height: 1.2; margin: 0 0 1rem; text-wrap: balance; }
      p { margin: 0 0 1rem; color: #b9c3e6; }
      a.go {
        display: inline-block; margin-top: .5rem; padding: .7rem 1.1rem; border-radius: 10px;
        background: #8fb4ff; color: #0b1020; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none;
      }
      a.go:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid #fff; outline-offset: 2px; }
      code { background: #1b2340; padding: .15rem .4rem; border-radius: 4px; font-size: .9em; }
      .sub { font-size: .92rem; color: #8b96bd; border-top: 1px solid #1b2340; margin-top: 1.5rem; padding-top: 1rem; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <h1>The interactive builder is now part of <span style="color:#8fb4ff">wicked-studio</span>.</h1>
      <p>
        Documents, presentations and demos are built in studio — the orchestrator IDE where product
        work gets done. You are being redirected.
      </p>
      <p><a class="go" href={TARGET}>Go to wicked-studio →</a></p>
      <p class="sub">
        <code>wicked-interactive</code> continues as the <strong>engine</strong> behind that surface — doc storage and version lineage, <code>data-wid</code> anchoring,
        HTML/PDF/PPTX export, and Playwright demo recording. wicked-crew runs it as a local bridge
        and proxies it; you no longer install or visit it directly.
      </p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
